# L §6.1 "A file that doesn't match its hash is refused (LOAD-PIN)"; L §8.3 LOAD-PIN "<file> doesn't match its sha256 in
# use <a>". Run with pin=bytes; the hash stated is of other bytes (one digit changed).
=== options pin=bytes
=== joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "ana.tally" sha256 "caf5f7622e7fa75fe10974cb18199597c91e70a92e887654d54870c36f543c68"

ask r: a.rate
=== ana.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
input rate: num

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  rate = 0.12 "umowa"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-PIN ana.tally doesn't match its sha256 in use a
